  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing SPS barriers to agricultural and fishery trade in the Caribbean</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: white;&quot;&gt;This action seeks to improve food-processing capabilities, to increase regional distribution in the Caribbean, addressing sanitary and phytosanitary (SPS) barriers and solutions to intra-regional trade of agricultural and fisheries products (including on traceability and circular economy processes). &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The proposed intervention aims at strengthening AHFS systems to reduce SPS bottlenecks impacting intra-regional trade; namely:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;i) Inadequate enforcement and implementation of SPS controls due to limitations in the regulatory framework.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;ii) Delays in applying SPS controls due to inefficiencies in the operations of Competent Authorities (CAs).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;iii) Limitations in the capability and capacity of competent authorities to enforce SPS controls (inspection, certification, testing and accreditation in agriculture and fisheries).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;iv) Limitations in the capacity of private sector stakeholders to implement SPS measures required for entry into local and regional markets (fisheries and agriculture).&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
